// The two questions a caller asks that are not "what is in the buffer".

// Where the caret is, as an index into the buffer. A caller that draws its own
// field -- one with a selection, or a different frame, or text at a per-mille
// scale -- needs this and tin_text() and nothing else from the drawing half.
tin_caret() {
} return int (import tin_st)[0];

// What the last tin_step came to, asked again. tin_step already answers it; this
// is for the caller whose drawing code is not the code that stepped, which is
// every caller with a frame loop that separates update from draw.
tin_act() {
} return int (import tin_st)[4];
